  "slug": "lipid-composition-c3e1",
  "summary": "New simulation and theory work spans Martini glycoproteins, filament assembly and pressure- or osmolyte-driven protein stability, extending multiscale structural modelling.",
  "synthesis": "The items share a multiscale, physics-based treatment of protein structure and assembly, with the dominant thread being coarse-grained or reduced models of how proteins organize and respond to their environment. GlycoMarinate automates Martini 3 modelling of N-glycoproteins, while a shape-based rigid-body model with interface-specific sites simulates PFKL filament assembly. Multiscale atomistic and coarse-grained MD with trajectory decomposition maps Histatin 1 self-association as multivalent and aromatic-driven. Complementary thermodynamic and theoretical work adds a pressure-dependent desolvation potential linking topology to collapsibility, and additive transfer m-values contrasting crystal disassembly with denaturation in osmolytes. An information-theoretic analysis of PrPC simulations identifies hot-spots and communication pathways. Together these extend environment-aware and transferable modelling, though the items address distinct systems.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
